#: ../../md/mlip.rst:4
msgid "機械学習原子間ポテンシャル"
msgstr "Machine-Learning Interatomic Potentials"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:6
msgid ""
"機械学習原子間ポテンシャル（machine-learning interatomic potential, MLIP）は、 "
"原子配置とセルからポテンシャルエネルギーを予測する。参照データに 第一原理計算を使う場合、新しい構造ごとに電子状態を解き直す計算を "
"学習済みモデルの評価に置き換えられる。多くの構造を緩和したり、 長い\\ :ref:`分子動力学<molecular-dynamics>`\\ "
"の軌跡を生成したりできる。 結果の精度は、どの配置をどの参照手法で学習したかに依存する。"
msgstr ""
"A machine-learning interatomic potential (MLIP) predicts the potential "
"energy from the atomic configuration and the cell. When the reference "
"data come from first-principles calculations, evaluating the trained "
"model can replace solving for the electronic state of each new structure."
" This makes it possible to relax many structures or generate long \\ "
":ref:`molecular dynamics <molecular-dynamics>`\\  trajectories. The "
"accuracy depends on which configurations were used for training and which"
" reference method produced the data."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:13
msgid "この記事では、エネルギー・力・応力の関係を確認し、学習データから 適用できる範囲を読み取り、目的に合う検証を選ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"This article examines the relation between energy, forces, and stress, "
"explains how to infer the range of applicability from the training data, "
"and shows how to choose tests suited to the intended use."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:17
msgid "原子配置からエネルギー・力・応力を求める"
msgstr "Calculating Energies, Forces, and Stress from Atomic Configurations"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"原子位置の組を :math:`\\boldsymbol R`、セルの基底を列に持つ行列を :math:`A`、モデルのパラメータを "
":math:`\\theta` とする。エネルギー :math:`U_\\theta(\\boldsymbol R,A)` "
"を予測するモデルでは、その微分から 原子 :math:`i` の力 :math:`\\boldsymbol F_i` とセルの応力が求まる。 体積"
" :math:`V` のセルを微小ひずみ :math:`\\boldsymbol\\varepsilon` で変形し、 "
"原子の分率座標を保つと、引張を正とした応力 :math:`\\sigma_{ab}` は"
msgstr ""
"Let :math:`\\boldsymbol R` be the set of atomic positions, :math:`A` the "
"matrix whose columns are the cell basis vectors, and :math:`\\theta` the "
"model parameters. If the model predicts the energy "
":math:`U_\\theta(\\boldsymbol R,A)`, its derivatives give the force on "
"atom :math:`i`, denoted :math:`\\boldsymbol F_i`, and the stress in the "
"cell. For a cell of volume :math:`V`, apply a small strain "
":math:`\\boldsymbol\\varepsilon` while keeping the fractional coordinates"
" of the atoms fixed. With tension taken as positive, the stress "
":math:`\\sigma_{ab}` is given by"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:26
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\left.\\frac{\\partial U_\\theta}\n"
"   {\\partial\\boldsymbol r_i}\\right|_A,\\qquad\n"
"\\sigma_{ab}=\\left.\\frac{1}{V}\n"
"   \\frac{\\partial "
"U_\\theta}{\\partial\\varepsilon_{ab}}\\right|_{\\boldsymbol\\varepsilon=0}"
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\left.\\frac{\\partial U_\\theta}\n"
"   {\\partial\\boldsymbol r_i}\\right|_A,\\qquad\n"
"\\sigma_{ab}=\\left.\\frac{1}{V}\n"
"   \\frac{\\partial "
"U_\\theta}{\\partial\\varepsilon_{ab}}\\right|_{\\boldsymbol\\varepsilon=0}"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:34
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`a,b` は直交座標の成分を表す。原子を動かしたときの エネルギーの傾きが力に、セルをひずませたときの傾きが応力に対応する。"
" 有限温度のMDで使う全応力には、この配置に由来する項に加え、 運動量の寄与が入る。"
msgstr ""
"The indices :math:`a,b` denote Cartesian components. The force is related"
" to the energy slope when atoms move, and the stress to the energy slope "
"when the cell is strained. The total stress used in finite-temperature MD"
" includes a momentum contribution in addition to this configurational "
"term."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:39
msgid ""
"多くのモデルは、全エネルギーを原子ごとの寄与の和として表す。各寄与は 近傍の原子種と原子間の相対配置で決まる。回転・並進や、同種原子の番号の "
"付け替えによって、全エネルギーが変わらないようにモデルを作る。 近傍に範囲を限る表現では、相互作用がその範囲を超えて効く場合に、 "
"電荷や長距離相互作用の別の表現が必要になることがある [MlipBehler2007]_ [MlipDrautz2019]_。"
msgstr ""
"Many models express the total energy as a sum of per-atom contributions. "
"Each contribution depends on the neighboring species and their relative "
"positions. The models are constructed so that rotations, translations, "
"and relabeling atoms of the same species leave the total energy "
"unchanged. A representation limited to a local neighborhood may require a"
" separate representation of charges or long-range interactions if "
"interactions extend beyond that neighborhood [MlipBehler2007]_ "
"[MlipDrautz2019]_."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:49
msgid "学習データが決める適用範囲"
msgstr "How Training Data Determine the Range of Applicability"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:51
msgid ""
"参照計算から得た構造、エネルギー、力、必要に応じて応力を組にして学習する。 エネルギーには配置ごとの安定性、力には個々の原子の変位に対する傾き、 "
"応力には変形に対する傾きの情報がある。参照に密度汎関数理論（DFT）を使うと、 "
"その交換相関汎関数や計算条件で得たエネルギー面を近似することになる。 力や応力が参照DFTに近くても、実験との差には参照DFTの近似も含まれる。"
msgstr ""
"Training uses structures, energies, forces, and, when needed, stresses "
"from reference calculations. Energies carry information about the "
"stability of each configuration, forces about the energy slopes under "
"individual atomic displacements, and stresses about the energy slopes "
"under deformation. With density functional theory (DFT) as the reference,"
" the model approximates the energy surface obtained with the chosen "
"exchange-correlation functional and calculation conditions. Even when the"
" forces and stresses agree closely with the reference DFT, differences "
"from experiment also reflect the approximations in that reference."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:57
msgid ""
"汎用モデルは多くの元素の組み合わせや構造を参照データに含む。 系に特化したモデルは、目的の材料の相・ひずみ・欠陥などを優先して学習する。 "
"たとえば原子クラスター展開（atomic cluster expansion, ACE）は、 原子の周りの多体配置を基底関数で展開する枠組みである"
" [MlipDrautz2019]_。 多体の情報を使って原子間で特徴を伝えるMACEを、広いデータで学習した後、 "
"対象材料の参照計算で追加学習する方法もある。この追加学習を **微調整** と 呼ぶ [MlipBatatia2022]_ "
"[HeatChen2025]_。"
msgstr ""
"General-purpose models include many combinations of elements and many "
"structures in their reference data. System-specific models prioritize "
"configurations representing phases, strains, defects, and other features "
"of the target material. For example, the atomic cluster expansion (ACE) "
"is a framework that expands many-body configurations around an atom in "
"basis functions [MlipDrautz2019]_. MACE passes features between atoms "
"using many-body information. One approach is to train MACE on a broad "
"dataset, then continue training on reference calculations for the target "
"material. This additional training is called **fine-tuning** "
"[MlipBatatia2022]_ [HeatChen2025]_."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:65
msgid ""
"含まれる元素が同じでも、高温の液体、結晶、表面、圧縮したセルは、原子の 近接環境が異なる。学習した環境の範囲から外れた配置への予測を外挿という。 "
"構造探索や昇温計算では、出発構造の近くで精度を確認したモデルでも、 途中で未学習に近い環境を通ることがある。利用する温度・圧力・組成と、 "
"現れうる構造を考えて、参照データと検証構造を選ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"Even with the same elements, a high-temperature liquid, a crystal, a "
"surface, and a compressed cell have different local atomic environments. "
"Predicting configurations outside the range of environments seen in "
"training is extrapolation. During a structure search or heating "
"simulation, even a model validated near the starting structure may "
"encounter environments barely represented in training. Choose reference "
"data and validation structures in view of the temperatures, pressures, "
"and compositions of interest and the structures that can occur."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:71
msgid ""
"MLIPが出すエネルギーの基準は、参照計算の出力や学習時の元素別オフセットに "
"依存する。異なるモデルの全エネルギーの表示値を直接引くと、その基準の差も入る。 比較には\\ :ref:`化学式単位あたりの相対エネルギー"
"<energy-reference>`\\ を使う。"
msgstr ""
"The MLIP energy reference depends on the reference calculation output and"
" the offsets assigned to individual elements during training. Directly "
"subtracting the reported total energies of different models also includes"
" the difference in their energy references. Compare \\ :ref:`relative "
"energies per formula unit <energy-reference>`\\ ."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:78
msgid "調べたい性質ごとに検証する"
msgstr "Validating the Properties of Interest"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:80
msgid ""
"参照データの一部を学習に使わず、モデルが見ていない構造でエネルギー・力・ "
"応力の誤差を求める。同じ軌跡の近い時刻のフレームは似ているため、ランダムに 振り分けるだけでは、未知の相やひずみに対する性能を見積もりにくい。 "
"別の軌跡や相から検証データを取ると、用途に近い予測を評価できる。"
msgstr ""
"Hold out part of the reference data and calculate errors in energies, "
"forces, and stress for structures the model has never seen. Frames close "
"in time within the same trajectory are similar, so a random split alone "
"makes it hard to estimate performance on unseen phases or strains. Using "
"validation data from other trajectories or phases lets you assess "
"predictions closer to the intended use."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:85
msgid ""
"力の誤差を全原子で平均した値だけでは、似た相どうしの小さなエネルギー差や、 変位の方向によるエネルギー曲線の違いを捉えたかどうかは分からない。 "
"相転移を目的とする場合は、用途に対応する量で検証する。"
msgstr ""
"The force error averaged over all atoms alone cannot show whether the "
"model captures small energy differences between similar phases or "
"differences between energy curves for different displacement directions. "
"For a phase transition study, validate the model using quantities "
"relevant to the transition."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:93
msgid "検証する量"
msgstr "Validation quantity"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:94
msgid "分かること"
msgstr "What it reveals"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:95
msgid "0 Kの相対エネルギー"
msgstr "Relative energies at 0 K"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:96
msgid "各相の静的な安定性の順序とその差を捉えたか。"
msgstr ""
"Whether the model captures the static stability ranking of the phases and"
" the energy differences between them."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:97
msgid "小変位・大変位でのエネルギー曲線"
msgstr "Energy curves at small and large displacements"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:98
msgid "平衡付近の曲率と、大きな変形に対するエネルギー上昇を捉えたか。"
msgstr ""
"Whether the model captures the curvature near equilibrium and the energy "
"increase at large deformations."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:99
msgid "昇温時に現れる相と見かけの転移温度"
msgstr "Phases observed during heating and apparent transition temperatures"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:100
msgid "指定したセル・時間・温度条件で構造変化を再現したか。"
msgstr ""
"Whether the model reproduces structural changes under the specified cell,"
" time, and temperature conditions."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:105
msgid "説明用の事例：BaTiO₃で三つの検証量を比べる"
msgstr "Worked Example: Comparing Three Validation Quantities for BaTiO₃"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:107
msgid ""
"BaTiO₃では、あるMLIPが静的な相の順位を再現しても、昇温軌跡に同じ相が "
"現れるとは限らない。CHGNetの公開事例を使い、静的な順位、一つの変位に 沿ったエネルギー、昇温時の構造変化を順に比べる。"
msgstr ""
"Even if an MLIP reproduces the static phase ranking of BaTiO₃, the same "
"phases may not appear in the heating trajectory. The published CHGNet "
"calculation examples illustrate three comparisons in turn: static phase "
"ranking, energy along one displacement, and structural changes during "
"heating."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:111
msgid ""
"**静的なエネルギー順位。** `BaTiO₃の安定基底状態 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/stability.html>`__ では、各相で最適化した格子を固定し、原子を緩和して0 "
"Kのエネルギーを比べた。 CHGNet 0.3.0を使ったLAMMPS計算では、菱面体晶を基準に "
"直方晶（斜方晶）が0.763、正方晶が5.043、立方晶が64.320 meV/化学式単位だけ "
"高かった。モデルはこの条件の4構造の中で菱面体晶を最も低く評価した。"
msgstr ""
"**Static energy ranking.** In the `BaTiO₃ stable ground-state calculation"
" example <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/stability.html>`__, the atoms were relaxed "
"with each phase's optimized lattice held fixed, and the energies at 0 K "
"were compared. In the LAMMPS calculation with CHGNet 0.3.0, the "
"orthorhombic, tetragonal, and cubic phases lay 0.763, 5.043, and 64.320 "
"meV per formula unit above the rhombohedral phase, respectively. Under "
"these conditions, the model ranked the rhombohedral phase lowest among "
"the four structures."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:117
msgid ""
"**変位に沿ったエネルギー。** `二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 1 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.html>`__ "
"では、各手法で求めた基準格子定数 :math:`a_0` の立方晶セルを使い、 Tiだけを :math:`[001]` "
"方向に動かした。事例の入力例に示された :math:`a_0` は、OpenMXで4.020 Å、SevenNetで4.035 "
"Å、CHGNetで4.036 Åである。 それぞれの格子で変位ゼロから極小までのエネルギー低下は、OpenMXのPBE計算で "
"6.16、CHGNet 0.3.0で1.69 meV/化学式単位だった。CHGNetの井戸はOpenMXの "
"約27%の深さだった。この比には両手法の格子定数の違いも含まれる。"
msgstr ""
"**Energy along a displacement.** In the calculation example `Double-Well "
"Potential, Part 1 <https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3"
"/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.html>`__, a cubic cell with the reference lattice "
"constant :math:`a_0` obtained by each method was used, and only Ti was "
"displaced along :math:`[001]`. The input examples give :math:`a_0` values"
" of 4.020 Å for OpenMX, 4.035 Å for SevenNet, and 4.036 Å for CHGNet. For"
" the respective lattices, the energy drops from zero displacement to the "
"minimum were 6.16 meV per formula unit for the OpenMX PBE calculation and"
" 1.69 meV per formula unit for CHGNet 0.3.0. The CHGNet well was about "
"27% as deep as the OpenMX well. This ratio also reflects the difference "
"between the lattice constants used by the two methods."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:125
msgid ""
"井戸の深さと、中心付近の力の変化は独立に調べる。変位を :math:`x`、 小さい変位幅を :math:`\\Delta x` とする。:eq"
":`mlip-energy-derivatives`\\ で 力は負の一次微分なので、曲率は力の傾きからも得られる。"
msgstr ""
"Examine the well depth and the change in force near the center "
"independently. Let :math:`x` denote the displacement and :math:`\\Delta "
"x` a small displacement increment. In Equation :eq:`mlip-energy-"
"derivatives`\\ , the force is the negative first derivative of energy, so"
" the curvature can also be found from the slope of the force:"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:129
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\left.\\frac{d^2 U}{dx^2}\\right|_{0}\n"
"    \\simeq \\frac{U(+\\Delta x)-2U(0)+U(-\\Delta x)}{(\\Delta x)^2},\\\\"
"\n"
"\\left.\\frac{d^2 U}{dx^2}\\right|_{0}\n"
"    \\simeq-\\frac{F_x(+\\Delta x)-F_x(-\\Delta x)}{2\\Delta x}.\n"
"\\end{gathered}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\left.\\frac{d^2 U}{dx^2}\\right|_{0}\n"
"    \\simeq \\frac{U(+\\Delta x)-2U(0)+U(-\\Delta x)}{(\\Delta x)^2},\\\\"
"\n"
"\\left.\\frac{d^2 U}{dx^2}\\right|_{0}\n"
"    \\simeq-\\frac{F_x(+\\Delta x)-F_x(-\\Delta x)}{2\\Delta x}.\n"
"\\end{gathered}"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:139
msgid ""
"中心近くの変位点を追加すれば、小変位で力が戻す向きか、さらに押し出す向きかを "
"判定できる。大きい変位点を追加すれば、井戸の外側でエネルギーが増える様子を 調べられる。極小の深さの比だけから曲率の比を求めることはできない。"
msgstr ""
"Additional points near the center show whether the force at small "
"displacements pushes back toward the center or farther away. Additional "
"points at large displacements show how the energy rises outside the "
"wells. The ratio of well depths alone cannot determine the ratio of "
"curvatures."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:143
msgid ""
"二つの曲線の形がなぜ独立に変わるかを、無次元の変位 :math:`u` と 無次元のエネルギー :math:`w_1,w_2` "
"で示す。第一の曲線に、中心と 極小ではゼロになる非負の項を足して第二の曲線を得る。"
msgstr ""
"To see why the shapes of the two curves can change independently, use the"
" dimensionless displacement :math:`u` and dimensionless energies "
":math:`w_1,w_2`. Add a nonnegative term that vanishes at the center and "
"at the minima of the first curve to obtain the second curve:"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:147
msgid ""
"w_1(u)=-2u^2+u^4,\\qquad\n"
"w_2(u)=w_1(u)+u^2(u^2-1)^2."
msgstr ""
"w_1(u)=-2u^2+u^4,\\qquad\n"
"w_2(u)=w_1(u)+u^2(u^2-1)^2."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:153
msgid ""
"両曲線は :math:`u=0` で0、:math:`u=\\pm1` で :math:`-1` になる。 "
"追加項は他の点でエネルギーを下げないので、極小の位置と深さはそのままである。 中心付近では追加項の主要部は :math:`u^2` "
"である。中心での二階微分 :math:`w_1''(0)=-4` にこれが2を加えるため、:math:`w_2''(0)=-2` になる。 :eq"
":`mlip-energy-curvature`\\ に相当する中心差分を :math:`\\Delta u=0.01` "
"で評価しても、曲率はそれぞれ約−4.000と−2.000になる。"
msgstr ""
"Both curves are zero at :math:`u=0`. At :math:`u=\\pm1` both have value "
":math:`-1`. The added term does not lower the energy at any other point, "
"so the positions and depths of the minima stay the same. Near the center,"
" the leading part of the added term is :math:`u^2`. It adds 2 to the "
"second derivative :math:`w_1''(0)=-4` at the center, giving "
":math:`w_2''(0)=-2`. Evaluating the central differences corresponding to "
"Equation :eq:`mlip-energy-curvature`\\  with :math:`\\Delta u=0.01` also "
"gives curvatures of about −4.000 and −2.000, respectively."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:160
msgid ""
"井戸の外側の :math:`u=2` では、第一の曲線は8、第二の曲線は44である。 "
"中心の曲率、極小の深さ、大変位での壁は、変位曲線の別々の性質を表す。 ここでの関数は読み方を示す模型である。"
msgstr ""
"Outside the wells, at :math:`u=2`, the first curve has value 8 and the "
"second 44. The curvature at the center, the depth of the minima, and the "
"walls at large displacements describe different properties of the "
"displacement curves. These functions are an illustrative model for "
"interpreting those properties."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:164
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-mlip-two-wells`\\ の左の拡大図では、中心付近の二つの曲線は "
"曲がり方が違うが、両側の極小では重なる。右では変位の範囲を広げており、 井戸の外側では差がさらに大きくなる。実際のモデル比較でも、用途に応じて "
"中心付近と大変位側の両方の点を取り、何を再現できたかを判断する。"
msgstr ""
"In the close-up on the left of :numref:`fig-mlip-two-wells`\\ , the "
"curves have different curvature near the center but coincide at the "
"minima on either side. The right panel covers a wider displacement range,"
" where the curves diverge even more outside the wells. In comparisons of "
"actual models, sample points near the center and at large displacements "
"as appropriate for the application to determine which features the models"
" reproduce."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:169
msgid "中心の曲率と大変位でのエネルギーが違う二つの曲線が、同じ位置と深さの極小をもつ。"
msgstr ""
"Two curves with different curvature at the center and different energies "
"at large displacements have minima at the same positions and depths."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:174
msgid "同じ深さの二重井戸。実線は第一の曲線、破線は第二の曲線。 左は中心付近、右は広い変位域を示す。丸印は両曲線に共通する極小。"
msgstr ""
"Double wells of equal depth. The solid line is the first curve, and the "
"dashed line is the second curve. The left panel shows the region near the"
" center, and the right panel shows a wider displacement range. The "
"circles mark the minima shared by both curves."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:177
msgid ""
"**昇温時の構造変化。** `BaTiO₃の構造相転移 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html>`__ では、Quloud "
"GPUのCHGNetで8 × 8 × 8のセルをNPTの温度・圧力制御のもと 10 "
"K/psで昇温した。最初に見えた構造は直方晶で、菱面体晶は軌跡に現れなかった。 正方晶から立方晶への見かけの転移は827 "
"Kで、記事が参照する実験値393 Kより 434 K高い。静的な順位から分かるのは試した構造のエネルギー差であり、 "
"昇温軌跡では有限温度での揺らぎ、緩和時間、モデルの力と応力が構造の遷移に効く。"
msgstr ""
"**Structural changes during heating.** In the `structural phase "
"transition calculation example for BaTiO₃ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html>`__, CHGNet on a Quloud "
"GPU heated an 8 × 8 × 8 cell at 10 K/ps under NPT temperature and "
"pressure control. The first structure observed was orthorhombic, and the "
"rhombohedral phase did not appear in the trajectory. The apparent "
"transition from tetragonal to cubic was at 827 K, 434 K above the 393 K "
"experimental value cited in the example. The static ranking tells us only"
" how the energies of the tested structures differ. In the heating "
"trajectory, finite-temperature fluctuations, relaxation times, and the "
"model's forces and stresses influence the structural transitions."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:187
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:189
msgid ""
"**参照と用途。** 参照DFTに近いエネルギー・力・応力は、学習したエネルギー面の "
"再現性を示す。実験と比較するときは参照DFTの近似、有限温度の計算条件、 模型の適用範囲も差に含まれる。"
msgstr ""
"**Reference and intended use.** Energies, forces, and stresses that agree"
" closely with the reference DFT indicate how well the model reproduces "
"the energy surface it was trained on. When comparing with experiment, the"
" difference also reflects the approximations of the reference DFT, the "
"finite-temperature calculation conditions, and the model's range of "
"applicability."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:192
msgid ""
"**小さい差の精度。** 全体で平均した学習誤差は、小さな相エネルギー差や特定方向の "
"力の誤差を隠すことがある。相の順位なら同じ条件の相対エネルギー、歪みに対する 応答なら応力や弾性の変化を調べると、用途に関係する誤差が見える。 "
"力を直接比べるには、昇温軌跡から取り出した同じ原子配置を各手法で :ref:`単点計算<structure-optimization>`\\ "
"する。別々に緩和した構造で力を比べる 場合と違い、比較に原子配置の差が入らない。"
msgstr ""
"**Accuracy of small differences.** A training error averaged over the "
"whole system can hide errors in small energy differences between phases "
"or in forces along specific directions. Relative energies under the same "
"conditions reveal errors relevant to phase rankings, while changes in "
"stress or elastic response reveal errors relevant to strain response. To "
"compare forces directly, perform a :ref:`single-point calculation "
"<structure-optimization>`\\  with each method for the same atomic "
"configuration taken from the heating trajectory. Keeping the "
"configuration fixed removes the differences in atomic configuration that "
"arise when the structures are relaxed separately."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:198
msgid ""
"**昇温時の比較。** モデルの差を調べるには、セルサイズ、昇温速度、保持時間、 "
"初期条件、判定法をそろえる。見かけの転移温度はこの比較の結果として扱い、 "
"平衡での境界を求めるには温度ごとの自由エネルギーや十分に緩和した分布が要る。"
msgstr ""
"**Comparisons during heating.** To isolate differences between models, "
"use the same cell size, heating rate, hold time, initial conditions, and "
"transition criterion. Treat the apparent transition temperature as an "
"outcome of this comparison. Finding the equilibrium boundary requires the"
" free energy or a sufficiently relaxed distribution at each temperature."

#: ../../md/mlip.rst:201
msgid ""
"**構造の適用範囲。** `Li₃PO₄の大規模構造とRDF <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/li3po4/large-structure-rdf.html>`__ "
"のような急冷構造では、結晶の格子定数に加え、 :ref:`部分動径分布関数<radial-distribution-function>`\\ "
"で原子種ごとの局所配位を 比べる。密度や配位の差が出れば、結晶の精度だけでは表せないモデル差を見つけられる。"
msgstr ""
"**Range of structures covered.** For quenched structures such as those in"
" the `large Li₃PO₄ structure and RDF calculation example <https://example"
".quloud-platform.quemix.com/li3po4/large-structure-rdf.html>`__, compare "
"local coordination by species using the :ref:`partial radial distribution"
" function <radial-distribution-function>`\\  alongside the crystal "
"lattice constants. Differences in density or coordination can reveal "
"differences between models that crystal accuracy alone does not capture."

